1
00:03:54,545 --> 00:04:00,545
Let the game begin...

2
00:07:49,090 --> 00:07:55,090
Escape Room is a horror, thriller, fantasy film directed by Peter Dukes.

3
00:11:43,636 --> 00:11:49,636
Four friends who partake in a popular Los Angeles escape room find
themselves stuck with a demonically possessed killer.

4
00:15:38,181 --> 00:15:44,181
They have less than an hour to solve the puzzles
needed to escape the room alive.

5
00:19:32,727 --> 00:19:38,727
Brice, played by Skeet Ulrich.

6
00:23:27,272 --> 00:23:33,272
Ramona, played by Sean Young.

7
00:27:21,818 --> 00:27:27,818
Jess, played by Christine Donlon.

8
00:31:16,363 --> 00:31:22,363
Jeff, played by Randy Wayne.

9
00:35:10,909 --> 00:35:16,909
Ben, played by Matt McVay.

10
00:39:05,454 --> 00:39:11,454
Angie, played by Ashley Gallegos.

11
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
Escape Room is a 2019 American psychological horror survival film 
directed by Adam Robitel from a screenplay by Bragi F.

12
00:46:54,545 --> 00:47:00,545
Schut and Maria Melnik, based on a story conceived by Schut.

13
00:50:49,090 --> 00:50:55,090
The film stars Taylor Russell, Logan Miller, Deborah Ann Woll, Tyler Labine, Nik Dodani, Jay Ellis, and Yorick van
Wageningen, and follows a group of people who are sent to navigate a series of deadly escape rooms.

14
00:54:43,636 --> 00:54:49,636
Development of the film began in August 2017, then under the
title The Maze, and the casting process commenced.

15
00:58:38,181 --> 00:58:44,181
Schut and Melnik were hired to write the screenplay, and
Robitel was confirmed to be directing.

16
01:02:32,727 --> 01:02:38,727
Filming took place in South Africa in late 2017 through January 2018.

17
01:06:27,272 --> 01:06:33,272
Brian Tyler and Jon Carey were hired to compose the
film's score, with Tyler also conducting.

18
01:10:21,818 --> 01:10:27,818
Escape Room was released in the United States on January 4, 2019,
by Columbia Pictures (via Sony Pictures Releasing).

19
01:14:16,363 --> 01:14:22,363
It grossed over $155 million worldwide and received mixed reviews from critics, who praised its atmosphere, cast, and
production design, but criticized the familiar plot and its failure to take full advantage of its premise.

20
01:18:10,909 --> 01:18:16,909
It was followed by the sequel Escape Room: Tournament of Champions in 2021.

21
01:22:05,454 --> 01:22:11,454
The tone is dark and intense.
